# D (#601, the user's decision on #536, 2026-11-13): the class side of an
# extension's conformance takes R0's candidates for a module's class
# method: the extension's own, then the target's own class-side dispatch
# in its order (`World::class_side_order`: its class methods, the modules
# it includes, then a superclass's with its includes; #669's decision,
# option 1, 2026-11-14), then a module a later include of the extension
# brings (#523), then a module another include of the extension brings (an
# earlier one, or through an include). So the target's own include comes
# before a later include of the extension (cell 9, which D had the other
# way) and before a superclass's method (cell 15, #669's reproducer, for
# the class and a subclass: what `C15.label` runs), and a module's class
# method with a body stays its own default beside another include's of
# the name (cell 14: the extension's other includes serve abstract
# requirements only, as R0's). Each line is the witness the rule gives,
# called through a `Type[R]` value; a scoped extension's (12, 13) runs
# where it is active and elsewhere alike (the class side's witness is
# fixed, #504).
# Accepted before D: 1, 2, 3, 5 (a module a later include brings), 8, 9,
# 14, 15; refused before ("must implement `self.label`"): 4, 6, 7, 10, 11,
# 12, 13. Answers #669 changed: 9 (was "9 later"), 15 (was "15 sup").
# Axes: target (class 1-9, 12, 13, 15; abstract class 10; generic class
# 11); source (own 1, superclass 2, later include 3, earlier include 4,
# brought 5, own include 6, superclass's include 7, precedence 8, 9, 15);
# scope (top-level 1-11, 15, scoped 12-13); backend (VM, and compiled by
# the build tests). Skipped: a module target (rule B refuses an extension
# of a module that includes).
module R1
  abstract def self.label -> String
end
class C1
  def initialize; end
end
extension C1
  include R1
  def self.label -> String = "1 own"
end
def via1(t: Type[R1]) -> String = t.label
module R2
  abstract def self.label -> String
end
class P2
  def self.label -> String = "2 sup"
end
class C2 < P2
  def initialize; end
end
extension C2
  include R2
end
def via2(t: Type[R2]) -> String = t.label
